'''The Harbingers''' is the achievement that unlocks {{e|Famine}}, {{e|War}}, {{e|Pestilence}}, and {{e|Death}} as four additional bosses. '''The Harbingers''' are referenced in the Bible as [[wikipedia:Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse|the Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse]]. These bosses are only unlocked once {{e|Mom}} has been defeated for the first time. These bosses, with the exception of {{e|Conquest}} and {{e|Headless Horseman}}, are guaranteed to drop either a {{i|Ball of Bandages}} or a {{i|Cube of Meat}}. By default, there is a 10% chance the current floor's boss will be a Harbinger unless the floor has a fixed boss (for example, {{e|Mom}} in {{s|Depths}} and {{s|Necropolis}}) or the Harbinger has been fought already. By using the {{i|Book of Revelations}} on a floor, it is guaranteed that the boss will be a Harbinger.

== Famine ==
{{e|Famine}} is the Harbinger for [[Chapter 1]].

[[File:Boss_Famine portrait.png|link=Famine]]

== Pestilence ==
{{e|Pestilence}} is the Harbinger for [[Chapter 2]].

[[File:Boss_Pestilence portrait.png|link=Pestilence]]

== War ==
{{e|War}} is the Harbinger for [[Chapter 3]]. War cannot be found in {{s|Depths}} II, {{s|Necropolis}} II, or {{s|Dank Depths}} II as {{e|Mom}} will always be the boss of that floor.

[[File:Boss_War portrait.png|link=War]]

== Death ==
{{e|Death}} is the Harbinger for [[Chapter 4]]. Death cannot be found in {{s|Womb}} II, {{s|Utero}} II, or {{s|Scarred Womb}} II as {{e|Mom's Heart}} or {{e|It Lives!}} will always be the boss of that floor.

[[File:Boss_Death portrait.png|link=Death (Boss)]]

== Conquest ==
{{e|Conquest}} is an alternative boss to {{e|Death}} in [[Chapter 4]]. He is unlocked once 10 items have been taken from {{r|Angel Room}}s. Conquest does not drop normal Horseman items, instead dropping {{i|White Pony}}.

[[File:Boss_Conquest portrait.png|link=Conquest]]

== Headless Horseman ==
{{e|Headless Horseman}} can appear in the place of any Harbinger. Like Conquest, he doesn't drop normal Horseman items, instead dropping {{I|A Pony}}.

[[File:Boss Headless Horseman portrait.png|frameless|link=Headless_Horseman]]

