== Trivia ==
* {{e|Conquest}} was added in the ''Binding of Isaac: Wrath of the Lamb''. In [[Wikipedia:Book of Revelation|the Bible]], Conquest is actually the first Horseman to appear, while {{e|Pestilence}} is a Horseman existing only in popular culture, coming from a different translation of the Greek word 'Thanatos', often meaning {{e|Death}} instead (the canon four Horsemen, thus, are Conquest, War, Famine and Death).
** {{e|Conquest}}'s entry in the secrets is called "The Forgotten Horseman", because of that very reason.
* {{e|Death}} is the only horseman specifically given a name in ''The Book of Revelation''.
* The use of the {{i|Book of Revelations}} item to summon a horseman for the current floor is reference to the fact that the book of the Bible in which the horsemen are described is Revelation.
* None of the Harbingers have a death animation.
* Under normal circumstances, {{e|Conquest}} and {{e|Headless Horseman}} are 2 of only 5 bosses (the others being {{e|Krampus}}, {{e|The Fallen}}, and {{e|Baby Plum}} if spared) who drop or can drop active items upon defeat.
** {{e|Bumbino}} can drop active items if paid 12 coins, but this does not defeat him in the traditional sense.
** As for abnormal circumstances, the use of {{t|Filigree Feather}} allows the Angels to drop active items, and the use of {{i|Satanic Bible}} allows nearly any boss to drop an active item.
* The horses used by the Harbingers resemble hobbyhorses.

